sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor A as Cluster / platform administrator
    participant PL as Platform provisioning service<br/>and guardrail controller
    participant AS as Agent Sandbox controller<br/>Red Hat build v0.9.0
    participant I as Identity issuer / token broker
    participant G as OpenShell gateway v0.1.10<br/>and Kubernetes driver
    participant O as TrustyAI operator
    participant CR as EvalHub custom resource
    participant E as EvalHub API instance

    Note over A,E: Phase 1 - cluster prerequisites, before the EvalHub operator
    A->>AS: Install Agent Sandbox v0.9.0 in openshift-operators
    A->>PL: Check OpenShift 4.19+, StorageClass and Kata
    A->>PL: Create gateway namespace and SA UID range
    A->>G: Install the pinned chart with the Route hostname in pkiInitJob.serverDnsNames
    G->>AS: Preflight the supported Agent Sandbox API
    A->>G: Configure workspace_mode shared and one static sandboxNamespace
    A->>I: Configure a qualified OIDC issuer with audience, subject and roles_claim
    G->>I: Validate audience, subject and role claim in RBAC mode
    A->>PL: Provision sandbox namespace guardrails
    PL->>PL: SCC/PSA, ResourceQuota, LimitRange, approved storage class
    PL->>PL: Egress NetworkPolicy baseline and exclusive control
    A->>G: Publish the baseline policy and template skeleton
    A->>PL: Distribute the gateway CA bundle
    PL->>PL: Mount it in the EvalHub namespace so the broker can verify the gateway
    PL->>PL: Prove Landlock and seccomp probes, egress and admission

    Note over A,E: Phase 2 - the platform publishes the gateway contract
    PL->>O: Publish openshell-gateway-info with qualified true, operator observes it
    Note over PL,G: The contract names endpoint, workspaceMode, sandboxNamespace and UID, versions, runtimeClass, storageClass and CA bundle. It never carries an administrator credential.

    Note over A,E: Phase 3 - instance enablement and readiness gates
    A->>CR: Create EvalHub with spec.sandbox.enabled true
    A->>CR: Set gatewayRef, profile, template, limits and providerBindings
    CR->>O: Admission webhook validates the contract, Kata, limits and credentials
    alt Admission rejects the custom resource
        O-->>A: Reject the CR, no half-configured instance
    else Custom resource accepted
        O->>O: Read the contract ConfigMap named by gatewayRef
        O->>O: Require qualified true, supported workspaceMode, UID and versions
        alt Contract missing, malformed or unqualified
            O->>CR: SandboxGatewayReady False and SandboxNamespaceAttested False
            Note over O,E: Sandbox dispatch stays off, /api/v1/info reports the reason and ordinary Job evaluations are unchanged
        else Contract qualified
            O->>CR: SandboxGatewayReady True and SandboxNamespaceAttested True
            O->>O: Create instance ServiceAccount, projected token and CA mount
            O->>I: Resolve the instance gateway identity
            alt Identity cannot be issued
                O->>CR: SandboxIdentityReady False, reason IdentityUnavailable
            else Identity issued
                O->>CR: SandboxIdentityReady True
                O->>O: Create and attest the adapter namespace guardrails
                O->>CR: SandboxAdapterNamespaceReady True
                loop Every namespace labelled evalhub.trustyai.opendatahub.io/tenant
                    O->>PL: Request tenant workspace and membership
                    PL->>G: Ensure workspace, membership, templates and bindings
                    G->>I: Validate the workspace role claim
                    PL-->>O: Return the workspace name and immutable UID
                    O->>CR: SandboxWorkspaceReady True, or SandboxWorkspaceFailed
                end
                O->>E: Render the sandbox block in the instance ConfigMap
                O->>E: Restart the API deployment with the rendered config
                O->>E: Report sandbox state and reason in /api/v1/info
                Note over O,E: Every ready condition true means sandbox-required providers may be enabled. Any false condition fails closed with no plain Job fallback.
            end
        end
    end
